From c71c8824e98da3bf8fd5187992958055498eb43b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Rudolph <patrick.rudolph@9elements.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Mar 2026 07:20:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] dts/aspeed: aspeed-bmc-ibm-system1: Fix PCIe slots

Currently the PCIe sensors readings aren't properly working. Update the
devicetree to resolve this problem.

* Add aliases for PCIe slots 1-8.
* Move PCIe slots 9-16 after PCIe slots 1-8.
  Keep existing non-PCIe bus numbers to not break user-space applications
  hardcoding I2C bus numbers.
* Add FRU EEPROMs
  Every PCIe slot is expected to have one specialized PCIe addon card
  that is equiped with a FRU EEPROM. The slots are non hot-plugable
  and all slots are always expected to be seated by such cards.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Patrick Rudolph <patrick.rudolph@9elements.com>
